er he Departed  the project in 2018 when pressed about  the reasons for leaving Whedon told  variety the story kind of just crumbled  in my hands there were elements that I  just hadn't mastered that after a long  time felt like I wasn't going to I told  people that I didn't have an idea which  isn't an exact truth I had an idea but  it didn't fit in the space that was left  for it but several years after that a  number of allegations about whedon's  Behavior towards the Justice League cast  spun out in the public sphere the  filmmaker eventually responded to the  criticism but he is still Persona on  grata in the DC film universe even  though Batgirl had been in development  for several years Leslie Grace wasn't  cast as Barbara Gordon until 2021  according to deadline naturally fans  spent a lot of time debating who should  play the Beloved bat family member with  Jane Levy being a name constantly  brought up in conversations in fact the  actor even used her Twitter account to  throw her name into the ring and drum up  some excitement for herself in the end  though the decision was between grace  and the White Lotus actor Hayley Lou  Richardson in an interview at The  Hollywood Reporter Richardson opened up  about the experience and about losing  out on the role she said I really tried  let me tell you I did get a nice little  personal email from JK Simmonds out of  it which was really nice getting the  role would have been pretty cool but I  told myself that his email meant more to  me than getting the role of course  Simmons reprized his Justice League role  as Jim Gordon Batgirl's father in the  film the Warner Brothers Discovery deal  had a huge impact on the DC Universe  News of the merger have been in the  pipeline for a while and it created  turbulence around the state of the dceu  since a regime change was on the horizon  and no one knew what the future held  there were Standalone films like Matt  Reeves the Batman and Todd Phillips  Joker but the status quo of the dceu was  always uncertain considering how plans  were subject to change at the drop of a  hat  fans found this whole scenario confusing  they weren't the only ones as it turns  out the filmmakers involved in these  projects also had no idea what was going  on but girl directors Adele lrb and  Bilal falar explained to the director  they weren't told which Universe their  film was set in lrb said we would also  ask oh you have JK Simmons from the  snyderverse and we got Michael Keaton  from the Burton verse what's the  situation there and they would say don't  worry about it we got a plan they never  really explained that aspect to us what  are the odds that Warner Brothers wasn't  sure about that either  the streaming walls are still upon us  and there seems to be no end in sight as  various platforms compete for similar  audiences and their subscriptions the  only way to win this battle is for the  streamers to provide the sorts of  content that viewers demand for HBO Max  the solution was to make platform  exclusive films like Batgirl as per The  Hollywood Reporter well the film didn't  have an Avengers like budget of 250  million dollars plus it still costly  reported 90 million dollars to produce  according to the rap entertainment  reporters Eric Davis and Umberto  Gonzalez held a session on Twitter  spaces where they discussed further  details about the movie according to  Gonzalez a source described a bad girl  as looking like something the CW would  have produced he recalled a source of  mindset I saw Batgirl certainly not the  worst superhero movie but ultimately I  understand why they canceled it I asked  this individual to elaborate a little  further and was told it's basically  essentially an expensive CW pilot which  is what I heard it was well that might  not be what fans wanted to hear about  film there's also no disputing that the  CW's arrowverse was a hit with audiences  even if it didn't feature a massive  budget Hollywood is like a Boulevard of  Broken Dreams it sells fantasies then  rips them away just as they're about to  come true since there is always a chance  that something will be canceled in the  pre-production phase most people in the  film industry don't believe anything  until it officially enters production  and the crew is on site bad girl however  proved to be one of the greatest  anomalies in the history of the business  Not only was 90 million dollars spent on  the film but it was also deep in  post-production before it received the  ax according to the Hollywood Reporter  the studio issued the following  statement about the cancellation the  decision to not release but girl  reflects our leadership strategic shift  as it relates to the DC Universe and HBO  Max it also helped the studio receive a  significant tax write-off as it embarked  on a cost-cutting exercise nonetheless  it shocked the world as no one has seen  such a high profile project get canceled  so close to the finish line an unnamed  exec from a rival Studio told film  reporter Justin Kroll that it was  something they'd never seen in 30 years  in the business the decision by Warner  Brothers Discovery to cancel Bagel  blindsided everyone especially since the  film was practically complete and as  part of a popular multimedia franchise  however many rumors have since surfaced  about what happened behind the scenes  that led to the movie's cancellation  including poor test screening scores  according to the New York Post the film  wasn't well received by test audiences  at all and the studio feared that  releasing the film would have been  irredeemable in the long run instead  Warner Brothers Discovery decided to hit  the eject button and ensure bad girl  would never be seen by moviegoers if you  won't let me help you what else can I do  and that said there have been  conflicting reports about the purported  low test scores The Hollywood Reporter  suggested that the film had only been  tested once in front of an audience and  received a rating in the low 60s which  would put it on par with other films  such as 2017's it and the upcoming  Shazam a fury of the Gods it was also  still without all its special effects  and the bells and whistles of a final  cut so the people in attendance would  have been watching a work in progress  rather than a completed version of the  film when Warner Brothers Discovery  pulled the plug on Batgirl it would seem  that the right thing to do would have  been to call up the casting crew and  explain the reasons that way they would  have all been prepared for when the news  broke in the media and all the questions  were fired in their Direction  unfortunately that wasn't the path the  studio chose leaving the crew just a  surprise by the film's cancellation as  everyone else I can't believe this  happening according to critical room the  crew was reportedly informed by the  studio to stop working on the film and  wait for further instructions however  the very next day they found out that  bad girl was canceled via social media  at the same time as everyone else  considering all the work they had done  on the movie and with no indication that  a cancellation was in the cards this  must have been the worst kind of  surprise for everyone who poured their  blood sweats and tears into the project  as soon as the news was officially  announced that bad girl was done for  there was a somberness in the air both  from fans and the people who worked on  the film The Sadness rippled across  social media as it felt like the loss of  a loved one or friend Batgirl was dead  and buried and nothing was going to  bring this film back from the grave to  close out the Saga Warner Brothers  Discovery reportedly held a screening  for the cast and crew and officially  dubbed the funeral screening according  to the Hollywood Reporter it allowed  everyone who was involved with the movie  one last chance to see the project that  they had worked so hard on after the  film was shown it was locked away in the  archives never to be discussed or seen  again it would be interesting to find  out if everyone wore black to the events  and brought Reese after the drama of  Zack Snyder's Justice League and the  vocal fandom that publicly targeted  Warner Brothers the studio was forced to  move in the direction of the release of  the Snyder cut but it didn't seem like  Warner Brothers was in the mood for  round two of that whole ordeal for  Batgirl as soon as the news broke that  the film was canceled the fans started  to rally on Twitter to see if they could  get another movement going to save  Barbara Gordon's Solo movie  unfortunately it appears as if the  studio wised up from the last time and  prevented the directors from even  teasing the possibility of it happening  in the future speaking to Entertainment  Weekly Adil el-abi and Bilal falal  confirmed that the film couldn't be  released as is since it required a few  more pickup shots and the addition of  visual effects however they wouldn't be  able to do so even if they wanted to  because they were logged out of  accessing the footage fala said we have  nothing Adele called me and said go  ahead and shoot some things on your cell  phone I went on the server and  everything was blocked it sounds like  Warner Brothers isn't messing around and  bad girl isn't Gonna See the Light of  day at least not any day soon  [Music]

